    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nThe Sweepstakes is one of Dublin's premier residential developments, fashionably located behind electronic security gates in the heart of Dublin 4. Built in 1992 by the highly regarded Cosgrave Builders, this beautiful home, which is flooded with natural light throughout, boasts spacious and well-appointed accommodation, is presented in turnkey order and is an ideal choice for those seeking a fashionable and secure home in Ballsbridge.\n \nNo 111 is a four bedroomed residence enjoying a prominent position at the back of this exclusive development. The accommodation briefly comprises a welcoming hallway with a guest w.c., and a most attractive spacious box bay windowed living room to the front of the property. The kitchen/dining room is very well equipped with a superb range of built in white high gloss wall and floor presses, the dining area overlooks the private rear garden and there is a separate utility room. Upstairs there are four generous sized bedrooms, the main bedroom is particularly impressive with a box bay window, a superb range of built in wardrobes and a modern ensuite shower room. There are three further double bedrooms all with built in wardrobes. The family bathroom completes the accommodation.\n \nThis lovely family home is further enhanced with a private back garden and a particularly large garage (c. 60 sq.m approx) with parking for several cars or it could be used as a home office or gym or for numerous other functions. The open plan garden to the front has off-street parking and there is also visitor parking.\nThis residence is the ideal choice for those seeking a secure home in Ballsbridge. The convenience of this location speaks for itself with local shopping in Ballsbridge not to mention a superb choice of coffee shops, restaurants and bars. Aviva Stadium, the RDS show grounds and Herbert Park are all within a short stroll and there is an excellent choice of public transport with Lansdowne DART station, a variety of bus routes available on Merrion Road including the Aircoach. Many of the city's principal places of business are within easy reach including Merrion Square, St. Stephens Green and the IFSC."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hallway: - \nbright and spacious with attractive flooring, ceiling coving and centre rose. T.V intercom. Double glass panelled doors to:\n\nCloakroom: - \nwith good storage.\n\nGuest w.c.: - \nwith w.c. and wash hand basin.\n\nLiving Room: - \nwith box bay window, attractive flooring, beautiful fireplace with coal effect gas fire. Ceiling coving, centre rose and built in shelving.\n\nKitchen/Dining Room: - \nsuperb bright and spacious room with an excellent range of built in white high gloss wall and floor presses. Integrated oven, hob and extractor fan. Integrated fridge freezer and dishwasher. Lovely dining area with views over the back garden, attractive flooring, breakfast counter. Access to the back garden.\n\nUtility Room: - \nwith built in wall presses, countertop, plumbed for washing machine and dryer. Good storage.\n\nUPSTAIRS - \n\n\nLanding: - \nbright and spacious landing with access to the attic. Intercom. Hotpress with good storage.\n\nMain Bedroom: - \nsuperb spacious and bright double bedroom with box bay window, floor to ceiling built in part mirrored wardrobes.\n\nEnsuite Shower Room: - \ndouble shower cubicle with rain forest shower head, w.c. and wash hand basin with underneath storage press. Fully tiled walls. Velux window.\n\nBedroom 2: - \nsuperb double bedroom with built in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 3: - \nsuperb double bedroom with built in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 4: - \nsmall double with built in wardrobes.\n\nFamily bathroom: - \nbath with shower attachment, w.c. and wash hand basin. Part tiled walls and tiled floor. Velux window.\n\n"
      },
